cff-version: 1.2.0

message: >
  If you use this software, please cite both the manuscript
  (Patil, 2026) and the software Concept DOI assigned by Zenodo.

type: software

title: Biofilm Poroelastic Simulation Code

version: 3.1.0

date-released: 2026-10-06

license: MIT

repository-code: "https://github.com/navinjpatil-J/biofilm-poroelastic-sim"

abstract: >-
  Python code for the manuscript "Interfacial drainage regime as a
  coordinate linking biofilm mechanics and transport". Three scripts
  regenerate Figures 1-6 and Supplementary Figure S1 and write the data
  plotted in each figure. The main script solves one-dimensional
  Biot/Terzaghi pressure diffusion with hard and leaky interior sinks,
  evaluates the Mandel-Cryer solution, and runs a synthetic
  model-recovery study.

keywords:
  - biofilm mechanics
  - poroelasticity
  - viscoelasticity
  - drainage regime
  - hydraulic permeability
  - extracellular matrix

